## Current versions

- **Laravel 13 is the current release.** Scaffold and target 13, not 12.

## Image generation (hard rules, measured 2026-09-14)

- **lora_scale 0.8, never 1.0.** At 1.0 a LoRA's own prior overrides the prompt (she comes back dressed). 0.70/0.85 were nude, 1.00 was clothed — same prompt, same seed.
- **Never put clothing words in `negative_prompt`.** They make the model DRAW clothing. Negative = limb/anatomy list only.
- **Anatomy list is mandatory** for nudes (bad anatomy, malformed, mutated, fused fingers, disfigured, deformed genitalia). A limbs-only negative is why genitals came out deformed.
- **Qwen-Image for NSFW identity work. FLUX mangles explicit anatomy** (extra limbs, morphed joints). FLUX LoRAs and Qwen LoRAs are architecture-locked — a Qwen LoRA cannot load into `flux-dev-lora`.
- **Beige thong on Qwen nudes (measured 2026-09-24):** regenerating with a bare-skin clause at lora 0.55–0.7 does **not** undress her. Existing keepers: `qwen-image-edit` in waves of **12** (50-wide sits at `starting`). New txt2img: scale 0.8 + `completely nude, no clothing, bare breasts with visible nipples`. Skill: `qwen-nude-beige-thong`.
- **codex / GPT-6 Astra cannot make NSFW** — moderation-blocked at the output stage. Don't try to route around it.
- **`--nude` is the default** on `amimage` / `jerimage` / `branimg`. `--no-nude` to dress. `--scale N` overrides.
- **A LoRA obeys only as well as its training set shape.** Needs: rare token, full angle rotation (front/front-left/front-right/back/back-left/back-right/lying/side), one named garment + named framing per short ~30-word caption, random scene and outfit. All close-ups = the model cannot render angles it never saw and falls back to clothed base priors.

## Preferences
- **Parallelism (HARD RULE, Jeremy 2026-09-14):** when using Replicate or ANY CLI, run **up to 50 jobs at once in parallel**. Never serialise a batch. Submit all predictions/processes up front, then poll. Applies to `amimage`/`jerimage`/`branimg`/Astra/codex/gemini/any generator or agent CLI.
- Max Parallelism.  Always use large workflows and fan out subagents.
