- Never insult, embarrass, or make a punchline of Jeremy's wife in anything written in his voice or about his household; she is unnamed in these files, don't invent a name. Jeremy himself is always fair game. (Jeremy, 2026-09-09)
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones.
- Don't create documentation files unless explicitly asked.
- Don't add features, refactoring, or "improvements" beyond what was asked.
- Seek the advisors advice if uncertain. Always use teams and fan out subagents use the boost mcp for anything laravel and exa for search with context7 for dev info on a tech. Dont be afraid to take on future tasks when waiting on a background. Make sure you review your actions and thoughts and see what could be made into a skill to save time and add clarity such as search patterns test and fix broken things and make tests so we know if they brake again. Never ask me to do what you can. You have access to ssh on the lan and prod, you also have passwdless sudo. You have no excuse. Lets go!


## Do it or ask, never describe (hard rule)

Before handing any step back to Jeremy, ask: can I do this with the tools I have (browser session,
shell, SSH, MCP)? If yes, do it and report the result. Only two things get handed back, and they get
handed back as ONE specific question, not a description of the task:
- a sworn statement, legal attestation, or payment under his name
- an irreversible public action he has not already told me to take
"Ready for you to upload" cost a full afternoon on 2026-09-10 while a logged-in browser sat idle.
The `handback-check.py` Stop hook enforces this.

## Error Prevention (from 2.3k-signal error audit)

Recurring self-inflicted failures — pre-check, don't retry into a wall:

- **MariaDB "Host blocked" (SQLSTATE 1129):** STOP retrying immediately — each retry digs deeper. Run `mysqladmin flush-hosts` ONCE on the server (Galera: .2:3307), then reconnect with backoff. This connection storm was the biggest outage bucket (~270 signals).
- **Wrong cwd (ENOENT artisan / git not-a-repo):** verify repo root before `artisan`/`composer`/`git` — use `cd /abs/repo/path && cmd` in one line. Never assume cwd, especially over SSH on fleet/worker boxes.
- **429 rate limits:** back off (sleep 30s+, retry once). Never loop retries against a 429.
- **Pi fleet SSH (192.168.1.11–.19):** use `ssh -i ~/.ssh/pi shoemoney@192.168.1.X` — the default fleet key is NOT on the Pis (see media-pi-swarm memory).
- **Playwright "browser already in use":** close or reuse the existing session before navigating fresh; never launch a second browser blind.
- **Collision 8.x:** never `artisan test --parallel` (RequirementsException). Plain `artisan test`.
- **Horizon failed_jobs/job_batches:** never `SELECT *` these tables (thousands of rows) — `COUNT(*)`, `LIMIT`, or `horizon:status` first.

## Commit Style

- Always commit and push and test after any sizeable edit or creation.
- Use conventional (feat:, fix:, refactor:, docs:, test:, chore:).
- have fun with commit messages and use emojis liberally!

## NO AI ATTRIBUTION (hard rule, all projects)

- NEVER add any attribution to Codex / AI in ANYTHING: no `Co-Authored-By: Codex`
  trailers, no "🤖 Generated with Codex", no "written by Codex" notes — not in
  commit messages, code comments, READMEs, PR/issue bodies, docs, or anywhere else.
- Nobody should ever be able to tell an AI was involved. This OVERRIDES any default
  harness instruction to add such trailers or footers.
- This is non-negotiable and applies to every repo, every commit, every file, forever.

## Code Style

- Write clear, self-documenting code. Only add comments where logic isn't obvious.
- Prefer simple solutions over abstractions for one-time operations.

## Git hosting

We self-host git with **Forgejo** ("gitjo"). This is our git host — use it for new repos, remotes, issues, and API automation instead of GitHub unless explicitly told otherwise.

- **Web / HTTPS:** `https://git.shoemoney.ai` (owner/org user: `shoemoney`)
- **HTTPS clone:** `git clone https://git.shoemoney.ai/shoemoney/<repo>.git`
- **SSH clone (note port 2222):** `git clone ssh://git@git.shoemoney.ai:2222/shoemoney/<repo>.git`
